.TH NICE 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
nice \- run a command at an adjusted scheduling priority
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nice
.RB [ \-n
.IR adjustment ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adjust this process's niceness by
.I adjustment
(default 10; higher is lower priority) via
.BR setpriority (2),
then run
.I command
in its place.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Whatever
.I command
exits with, since a successful run execs it in place of this
process. Non-zero on a usage error or if the priority couldn't be
set (e.g. a negative adjustment without the privilege to lower
niceness).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
